me>Mohammadi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephen</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comment: Medical education reform in Iran</article-title><source>Family Medicine</source><year>2003</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>616</fpage><lpage>617</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14523653</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pezeshkian</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Karimi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Akbari</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Einollahi</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosseini</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosseini</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Integration of medical education and health care: the experience of Iran</article-title><source>Journal of Medical Education (Iranian)</source><year>2003</year><volume>Spring</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walton</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Global demands on medical education: the case of Iran</article-title><source>Iranian Journal of Medical Education</source><year>2001</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ijme.ir/browse.php?mag_id=8&#x00026;slc_lang=fa&#x00026;sid=1"/></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mirzabegy</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Basiri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yadegarynia</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Zarein-dolab</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving medical education in Iran: an action research in changing the curriculum and teaching and learning methods</article-title><source>Journal of Medical Education (Iranian)</source><year>2001</year><volume>Spring</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blackburn</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Horowitz</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Edington</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name><name><surname>Klos</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>University faculty and administrator responses to job strains</article-title><source>Research in Higher Education (Historical Archive)</source><year>1986</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00991876</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blix</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Cruise</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>BMc</given-names></name><name><surname>Blix</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Occupational stress among university teachers</article-title><source>Educational Research</source><year>1994</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>169</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pareek</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Pareek U</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Organizational Role Stress</article-title><source>Pfeiffer's Classic Inventories, Questionnaires, and Surveys</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London: John Wiley</publisher-name><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>329</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pareek</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Pareek U</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The Role</article-title><source>Training instruments in Human Resource Development and Organisational Development</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>New Delhi: Tata McGraw-Hill</publisher-name><fpage>475</fpage><lpage>567</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pestonjee</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Azeem</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A study of Organizational Role Stress in relation to Job Burnout among university teachers</article-title><source>IIMA Working papers (Indian instituet of management Ahmedabad, Research and Publication Department)</source><year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lease</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Occupational role stressors, coping, support, and hardiness as predictors of strain in academic faculty: an emphasis on new and female faculty</article-title><source>Research in Higher Education</source><year>1999</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1018747000082</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maslach</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaufeli</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Leiter</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Job Burnout</article-title><source>Annual Review of Psychology</source><year>2001</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>422</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11148311</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1146/annurev.psych.52.1.397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kushnir</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitai</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Continuing medical education and primary physicians' job stress, burnout and dissatisfaction</article-title><source>Medical Education</source><year>2000</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>430</fpage><lpage>435</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10792682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2923.2000.00538.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gmelch</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilke</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lovrich</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dimensions of stress among university faculty: factor-analytic results from a national study</article-title><source>Research in Higher Education</source><year>1986</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>266</fpage><lpage>286</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00992075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thorsen</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress in academe: What bothers professors?</article-title><source>Higher Education</source><year>1996</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>471</fpage><lpage>489</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00137127</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dua</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Job stressors and their effects on physical health, emotional health, and job satisfaction in a university</article-title><source>Journal of Educational Administration</source><year>1994</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>59</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1108/09578239410051853</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harden</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress, pressure and burnout in teachers: is the swan exhausted?</article-title><source>Medical Teacher</source><year>1999</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/01421599979482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Stress in academic life: the mental assembly line</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name>Buckingham: Society for Research into Higher Education and the Open University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rutter</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Herzberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Paice</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress in doctors and dentists who teach</article-title><source>Medical Education</source><year>2002</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>543</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12047669</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2923.2002.01229.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lackritz</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><arti